cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PQID-Bench, please cite the benchmark release and the underlying
  PQID v1.0.2 dataset.
type: software
title: "PQID-Bench: A Validation-Aware Benchmark Suite for Quantum-Program Generation"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21649753"
date-released: "2026-07-23"
authors:
  - family-names: "Gasparini"
    given-names: "Elias Abebe"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum programming
  - Qiskit
  - code generation
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
repository-code: "https://github.com/Elias-Abebe-Gasparini/PQID-Bench"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21649753"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  PQID-Bench is a frozen validation-aware benchmark suite for quantum-program
  generation. Over its 21-model by 154-prompt primary matrix, 2,950 of 3,234
  outputs execute, 2,944 are OpenQASM 3 assembly admissible, and 1,703 recover
  the frozen reference signature. Its 38.37-point Assembly-Structure Gap
  retains 99.52% of the 38.56-point Execution-Structure Gap. The release also
  evaluates ordered operation-and-operand recovery, parameter-aware recovery,
  robustness, and stochastic repeatability.
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "PQID: Parallel Quantum Instruction Dataset (v1.0.2)"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Gasparini"
        given-names: "Elias Abebe"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20674853"
